  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response and Recovery Assistance to the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response and Recovery Assistance to the Philippines (RRAP) is an investment that supports the Philippine Government to respond to the humanitarian and early recovery needs of the most vulnerable people affected by disasters and conflict. RRAP:

1. provides appropriate and timely humanitarian and protection assistance to the most vulnerable people affected and displaced by disasters and emergencies; and 
2. supports households to recover and participate in local, sustainable, economic activities.

This program is delivered through UN agencies, Red Cross and Red Crescent societies and non-government organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
